<PageTitle>Development Rules - Opx MudBlazor Flat UI</PageTitle>

<FlatPage Kind="FlatPageKind.Module" UsePanel="false" PageCssClass="development-rules-page no-mobile-fab">
    <ChildContent>
        <section class="development-rules-intro" aria-labelledby="development-rules-heading">
            <span class="eyebrow">Source of truth</span>
            <h1 id="development-rules-heading">Build every page from the same contract</h1>
            <p>This showroom summarizes the repository rules and development skill. Read the canonical files before implementation, then use the matching sample page as executable reference.</p>
        </section>

        <div class="development-rules-grid">
            @RulePanel("1", "Resolve page identity", "Assign one unique PageId, route, PageTitle mapping, menu/search entry, and host-owned permission boundary. Use the canonical page registry before choosing an archetype.", "opx.page.<area>.<purpose>")
            @RulePanel("2", "Keep the AppBar authoritative", "Row one is AppName and row two is PageTitle. Do not repeat the page title or description in content unless the description is explicitly required. Keep the operational AppBar at 60px and center its 40px hamburger with equal 10px top and bottom space.", "AppName / PageTitle")
            @RulePanel("3", "Use responsive navigation deliberately", "Sidebar is the default. Horizontal is web-only; Bottom is phone-only. Sidebar parent, child, and deeper labels share one font size and normal weight through --opx-sidebar-item-font-weight; Horizontal and Bottom item labels are normal too. Bottom children use the configured Sheet default or Main View icon-and-text tiles, with recursive Back and safe-area gutters.", "Sidebar · Horizontal · Bottom · Weight 400")
            @RulePanel("4", "Compose grids from shared state", "Desktop tables and mobile cards share search, column filters, sort, paging, selection, and permissions. Global appsettings default table headers to CompactSearch with search/sort affordances visible and metadata/type icons hidden; each grid may deliberately override HeaderStyle or ShowHeaderIcons, including Standard for legacy filter-row presentation. Table presentation independently supports alternate rows (default off), vertical lines (default on), and horizontal lines (default on); mobile cards retain their own separators. AutoRowHeight is opt-in: non-numeric content wraps, the row grows to its tallest cell, all cells top-align, and numeric cells stay single-line/right-aligned. FlatGroupedDataGrid adds accessible expand/collapse groups and localized host-owned summary values without becoming a Pivot or calculating business totals. Filters open in a mobile sheet; bounded desktop grids own both scroll axes, while bounded Model CRUD cards own one internal vertical scroller with toolbar and pager fixed. An opt-in mobile edge status uses fixed responsive width and overlaps the card's top/right border by exactly one pixel. Mobile search toolbars keep search/filter text visible, place a transparent Apps/Close action-row toggle in the search placeholder area, and default the action row to collapsed/hidden; the complete touch target stays vertically centered against the search border box and never resembles a combo-box chevron or overflow menu. Lookup grids use ASC/DESC-only headers, search the active sorted column, autofocus search, and route modal letter/number typing into it.", "Grid: CompactSearch, icons off")
            @RulePanel("5", "Expose one primary action", "Writable CRUD uses one desktop Add button and one icon-only mobile FAB generated from the same FlatPage action. FAB shape comes from appsettings: Circle is default, Square is optional. On bounded mobile/tablet lists with a pager, the FAB sits in normal flow immediately below the pager and aligns right in Sidebar and Bottom-navigation layouts, so every pager control remains touchable. Toolbar filter, refresh, import, export, and custom actions stay icon-only and configurable.", "FlatPage PrimaryAction")
            @RulePanel("6", "Honor CRUD result contracts", "Use Edit—not Ubah—for the CRUD edit action, editor title, tooltip, and accessible label. Mobile editors are fullscreen. Browser or MAUI hardware Back closes the active modal before navigation or app exit. A dirty Back or Cancel opens the shared locked MessageBox; discard closes only the top modal and returns false without reload, while continue editing preserves the draft. Successful Create, Update, or Delete returns the exact result and may refresh the caller.", "Edit · Cancel = no refresh")
            @RulePanel("7", "Use theme-safe flat geometry", "Cards, panels, inputs, dialogs, menus, grids, toolbars, and workspaces stay square. Ordinary buttons default to 7 px through the global Rounded size setting (0-12 px), which also controls bottom-sheet top corners; semantic circles and FAB shape remain separate contracts. Fluent Blue is the default palette; Blue, Trust, Slate, Ocean, Emerald, and Rose remain selectable and resolve through shared typed Light/Dark tokens, Settings, and appsettings—never page-local CSS. Text buttons using MudBlazor's inherit contract keep their enclosing surface foreground, including DatePicker toolbar actions. Default portal tooltips own a neutral high-contrast background and foreground instead of inheriting a muted or disabled trigger color.", "DefaultRoundedSizePx: 7 · fluent-blue")
            @RulePanel("8", "Adapt instead of shrinking desktop", "Keep one Blazor codebase and one OPX design system, but transform navigation, hierarchy, forms, actions, and data presentation by viewport. FlatAppShell Bottom mode defaults to a 600px threshold; this sample explicitly sets 900px so tablet and phone use Bottom navigation while desktop uses the sidebar. When Bottom navigation is requested, child and overflow menus default to the package Sheet presentation; MainView is explicit opt-in only. Live resize, including Windows EXE, follows viewport width only—never OS, device type, user agent, or MAUI platform. Bottom labels preserve descenders through shared 1.25 line-height and a 1px bottom inset without increasing the 60px bar. Android MAUI alone uses host-owned edge-to-edge: the native status bar stays transparent, actual WindowInsets extend the AppBar to 60px plus inset, controls remain in the lower 60px, and theme/palette changes refresh status-icon contrast. Never hardcode status-bar height or apply this native geometry to Web/Windows.", "Default 600 · Sample 900 · Child Sheet")
            @RulePanel("9", "Keep typography and spacing coherent", "Font ownership defaults to Device/browser root size, but Settings always lets users persist Device or Manual. Manual reveals the bounded font slider; Device hides it without losing its last value. The spacing preset maps to package density and starts at Default; Compact and Comfortable remain choices, while Restore returns to Default. Appsettings supplies Restore defaults, not a UI lock. Settings/About headers and footers never shrink; the body alone scrolls so heading and supporting copy remain complete. Shared panel title/subtitle pairs use a compact 3px gap with bounded line heights. Font size and density remain independent. Entered form text uses the slightly smaller responsive --opx-type-input token without changing control geometry. Numeric values use one compact monospace token with tabular digits, while labels and headers keep the normal UI font. Mobile-card fact values use normal weight and only the primary identifier heading is emphasized. Every form-control placeholder matches its entered-value font size and weight. Mobile gutters remain 16px. Web refresh is per-page; Dashboard/DashboardList default on with a real handler and can opt out, while other pages opt in. MAUI Android/Windows may independently use NativePullToRefreshEnabled. CRUD modals suspend both gestures and closing restores the underlying list/dashboard state.", "Density: Default · Top-only · Modal suspended")
            @RulePanel("10", "Leave business ownership to the host", "The library owns presentation and typed callbacks. The host owns API calls, authorization, persistence, validation, concurrency, audit, upload storage, realtime/device integration, GPS, geocoding, and routing engines.", "Host-owned effects")
            @RulePanel("11", "Verify before release", "Run unit and component tests, desktop/responsive/phone live-resize checks, Light/Dark/Auto and accessibility checks, public API compatibility, Release build, package-content inspection, and fresh-consumer restore before publishing.", "Evidence before claims")
            @RulePanel("12", "Keep spatial state controlled", "Layered floors, geofences, work-list selection, viewport, and route playback use typed host-controlled state. Mobile stacks the list and map without page overflow; GPS, routing, geofence evaluation, and telemetry remain host-owned.", "FlatSpatialWorkspace")
            @RulePanel("13", "Use the global application foundation", "Protect unsaved drafts, express permission and feature visibility, normalize operation failures and server queries, persist workspace state through host providers, and keep session, telemetry, and accessibility intents explicit. Put the root startup gate before Router on anonymous and protected routes; render FlatSessionRestore inside the OPX providers/theme shell, then create Router only after the host check succeeds. Session bootstrap and Reconnecting share one system spinner. Web and MAUI host documents also provide a static themed fatal-error surface outside the circuit with one Restart action and no framework error details or Dismiss path; session validation remains host-owned.", "Root gate before Router")
            @RulePanel("14", "Reuse the Material icon picker", "Use FlatMaterialIconPicker for Filled and Outlined MudBlazor icons. Keep search and paging inside the shared responsive modal, and persist the stable icon name plus style instead of copying SVG values into business data.", "FlatMaterialIconPicker")
            @RulePanel("15", "Resolve one default input style", "Use the scoped Standard, Filled, or Outlined preference for MudBlazor and generated-form inputs. Outlined is the appsettings default. Settings live-previews and persists the user choice without static global state; explicit component variants remain deliberate overrides.", "DefaultInputStyle: Outlined")
            @RulePanel("16", "Resolve sidebar colors per theme", "Seed Light/Dark sidebar background and text from appsettings, then allow per-user live preview, Save, Cancel, and Restore in Settings. Normalize each #RRGGBB value independently, preserve semantic active/hover states, and target at least 4.5:1 text contrast.", "Four scoped sidebar colors")
            @RulePanel("17", "Separate outline design from Tree Grid", "Use FlatHierarchyDesigner for compact report bands, style trees, and configuration outlines. Stable key, parent, and order values produce exact before/inside/after move results; Web drag/drop is paired with accessible move actions, invalid cycles are rejected, and JSON export is a versioned snapshot. Editing and persistence remain host-owned.", "opx.page.reference.hierarchy-designer")
            @RulePanel("18", "Adapt Work Week scheduling", "Use FlatScheduler WorkWeek for appointment timelines. Desktop owns an internally scrolling calendar rail and time grid; tablet/mobile uses daily agenda groups and a calendar-options bottom sheet. The host owns conflicts, timezone conversion, recurrence, reminders, authorization, and persistence.", "opx.page.schedule.scheduler")
            @RulePanel("19", "Keep tablet card grids scrollable", "At 900px and below, the visible card list is the single bounded touch scroll owner. A pan that starts on card content must scroll the list in every theme and grid presentation mode, including tablet landscape and live resize. Pull-to-refresh only takes over for a downward gesture when the list is already at the top.", "opx.page.reference.large-data-grid")
            @RulePanel("19", "Choose the Login composition", "Keep LoginLayout Default for the established split desktop and compact mobile composition. Use Boxed for a centered bounded form over the configured brand background. Both modes reuse one form, theme/input preferences, responsive tokens, MessageBox feedback, and host-owned authentication; invalid values return to Default.", "opx.page.auth.login · Default / Boxed")
        </div>

        <FlatPanel Title="Canonical development path" Subtitle="Follow this order for every new or revised page" CssClass="flat-panel development-rules-flow">
            <ol>
                <li><strong>Read</strong><span><code>RULES.md</code>, <code>.agents/RULES.md</code>, and the development skill.</span></li>
                <li><strong>Resolve</strong><span>Find the PageId and archetype in <code>page-registry.md</code>.</span></li>
                <li><strong>Reuse</strong><span>Open only the relevant files listed by <code>sample-source-map.md</code>.</span></li>
                <li><strong>Implement</strong><span>Prefer package components and shared state instead of page-local behavior.</span></li>
                <li><strong>Verify</strong><span>Test Light/Dark/Auto, desktop/mobile, live resize, keyboard, overflow, and host callbacks.</span></li>
                <li><strong>Synchronize</strong><span>Update rules, skill references, documentation, sample, tests, and handoff when the contract changes.</span></li>
            </ol>
        </FlatPanel>
    </ChildContent>
</FlatPage>

@code {
    private static RenderFragment RulePanel(string number, string title, string copy, string contract) => @<article class="development-rule-card">
        <span class="development-rule-number">@number</span>
        <div>
            <h2>@title</h2>
            <p>@copy</p>
            <code>@contract</code>
        </div>
    </article>;
}
